[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646487016","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102536#issuecomment-2646487016","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102536","id":2646487016,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dvi_o","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-09T18:55:04Z","updated_at":"2025-02-09T18:55:04Z","body":"The problem is more radical, simply setting the Node3D scale to 0 causes the problem of `det == 0`.\n\nThis condition makes any interpolation-related calculations impossible because the direction of the axes (object orientation) cannot be determined.\n\nIt may be possible to work around it by treating it internally as a Vector3(0.001, 0.001, 0.001), but I don't think that should be done implicitly, as this could produce unintended calculation results.\n\nSince negative scale behavior is documented in Node2D, I would have thought that Node3D would have similar documentation, but I noticed that it does not. I think we can add documentation on this Zero-scaled case.\n\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/ja/4.x/classes/class_node3d.html#class-node3d-property-scale","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646487016/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646569095","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102536#issuecomment-2646569095","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102536","id":2646569095,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dv3CH","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-09T20:20:04Z","updated_at":"2025-02-09T20:20:04Z","body":"@TokageItLab actually, I think we can support zero-scaled objects as long as the don't require the inverse transform matrix. So we can support it for things like decals, but maybe not meshes","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/